-- 431: TY2025 Optional State Sales Tax Table (Schedule A line 5a).
--
-- Itemizers may deduct general sales tax INSTEAD of state income tax
-- (IRC 164(b)(5)). Most use the IRS optional table rather than receipts, and
-- ProConnect calculates that table amount itself — the export carries only
-- the inputs (election, actual receipts, special items, local rate). A client
-- in a state with no income tax therefore rendered Schedule A short by the
-- whole table amount. lib/forms/form-1040-estimates.ts reads this constant to
-- close that gap.
--
-- SOURCE: 2025 Instructions for Schedule A (Form 1040), "2025 Optional State
-- Sales Tax Tables", read from https://www.irs.gov/instructions/i1040sca on
-- 2026-10-11. Transcribed by script, not by hand: two independent parsers of
-- that page (a browser DOM walk and a Python html.parser pass) produced the
-- same SHA-256 over the amounts, 9008265dfa76ea476db409d244d6dab86efae87e54b8b41b868335ca646d9c4e.
--
-- SHAPE:
--   bands   lower bound of each income band ("At least"); the last band is
--           open-ended ("$300,000 or more"). Income = 1040 line 11 plus
--           nontaxable items.
--   states  by USPS code. 46 entries; AK, DE, MT, NH and OR have no state
--           general sales tax and therefore no table.
--     rate     state rate from the table heading, percent
--     amounts  one row per band, six columns = family size 1..5 and "over 5"
--     local    how the worksheet adds LOCAL sales tax (lines 2-6):
--       ratio                  table amount x local rate / state rate
--       ratio_over_table_rate  CA and NV: the table already includes a
--                              uniform local rate, so only the excess over
--                              `rate` is added, by the same ratio
--       local_table            AL AZ AR CO GA IL KS LA MS MO NY NC SC TN UT
--                              VA: a separate local table keyed by locality
--                              (not seeded — see the estimator)
--       none                   no local general sales tax
--
-- Applies to TY2025 only. A TY2024 table must be read from the 2024
-- instructions; the 2025 figures are the 2024 tables grown by state revenue
-- (IRS note under the table), so they are NOT interchangeable.

begin;

insert into form_1040_constants (tax_year, key, value, notes) values
